==English==

===Etymology===
From {{prefix|un|just|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ʌnˈdʒʌst/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-unjust.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
:* {{rhymes|ʌst|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Not [[fair]], [[just]] or [[right]].
#: ''The solution was very '''unjust'''.''

====Synonyms====
* [[unfair]]

====Antonyms====
* [[just]]

====Related terms====
* [[justice]]
* [[injustice]]

====Usage notes====
Beware that '''unjust''' and {{term|injustice|lang=en}} use different prefixes (French {{term|injustice|lang=fr}} was borrowed into English, but {{term|injuste|lang=fr}} was not). ''[[injust]]'' is archaic and ''[[unjustice]]'' is obsolete.

